---
description: Use Flatpack ViewComponents for dummy demos and library components
globs: "**/*.{erb,html,css,js}"
alwaysApply: false
---

This repo is Flatpack. These rules apply to dummy demos and library components.

Search https://flatpack.bowerbird.io/ and this repo before you write custom CSS or markup. Compose existing ViewComponents. Do not rebuild buttons, forms, alerts, cards, modals, or nav.

Semantic layout markup is fine when Flatpack has no structure for that part of the page.

If you need a piece Flatpack does not have, ask whether to add it here. Do not invent custom UI in silence.

Do not rewrite unrelated legacy UI just because you opened the file. When you touch a legacy element, migrate that element if the change is local and safe.

Use the core default layout. Dummy default is `html data-theme="rounded"` plus core `UsesDefaultLayout`. One primary action per page.

Which component and what lands: `flatpack-design`. Motion patterns: `flatpack-micro-interactions`. Do not restate those skills here.
